---
title: "redeem - Withdraw Asset from Lending Pool (Scallop Lend)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_check_version: check version == current_version
    q_check_version --> q_error_version: version mismatch
    q_error_version --> [*]: abort error
    q_check_version --> q_accrue_interest: version matches
    q_accrue_interest --> q_calc_rate: accrue_interest(market, clock)
    q_calc_rate --> q_calc_redeem: exchange_rate = total_supply / total_market_coin
    q_calc_redeem --> q_check_amount: redeem_amount = scoin_value * exchange_rate
    q_check_amount --> q_error_small: redeem_amount too small
    q_error_small --> [*]: abort 2050
    q_check_amount --> q_check_liquidity: redeem_amount valid
    q_check_liquidity --> q_error_liquidity: pool_liquidity < redeem_amount
    q_error_liquidity --> [*]: abort 81921
    q_check_liquidity --> q_check_reserve: pool_liquidity >= redeem_amount
    q_check_reserve --> q_error_reserve: reserve not enough
    q_error_reserve --> [*]: abort 81924
    q_check_reserve --> q_burn_scoin: reserve sufficient
    q_burn_scoin --> q_withdraw: burn MarketCoin
    q_withdraw --> q_update_pool: withdraw underlying from pool
    q_update_pool --> q_emit: total_supply -= redeem_amount
    q_emit --> [*]: emit RedeemEvent, return Coin

    note right of q_calc_redeem
        INV-001: redeem_amount = scoin_value * exchange_rate
        INV-002: exchange_rate used for redeem >= exchange_rate at mint time
    end note

    note right of q_burn_scoin
        INV-003: MarketCoin supply decreases by scoin_value after burn
        INV-004: pool_liquidity >= redeem_amount before withdrawal
    end note
